# What K816 compiles this fixture to, assembled with ca65 and linked with
# `../../atarixl.cfg`.  Sixteen bytes per line, load address in the left
# column; the zero fill past the last byte is trimmed.
#
# There is no oracle golden beside this one on purpose: the fixture is
# invented, and what it asserts is K816's *lowering* of a meaning the oracle
# already answered (`k65/align-and-address`).
#
# Read it as three placements:
#
#   $2000  .align $10 is already satisfied, .res $04 fills four bytes
#   $2004  table - congruent to 4 modulo 16, and the label follows the pair
#   $2007  three bytes of table, then .align $20 rounds to $2020
#   $2028  aligned - congruent to 8 modulo 32, again after the .res
#   $202B  main: lda $2004, jsr $2028, rts

origin 2000
2000  00 00 00 00 01 02 03 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
2010  00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
2020  00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 A9 01 60 AD 04 20 20 28
2030  20 60
